    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0594" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg468"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.2315/243a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Poindexter</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-10-30T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30,
                                1925—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>62. Department advised by Colombian Minister that Colombian Government has
                    ratified Colombian-Peruvian Boundary Treaty of 1922, thus complying with its
                    obligations under Section 2 of the Procès Verbal of March 4, last.<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d307-f1"/></p>
                <p>In the course of conversation today on other matters I informed the Peruvian
                    Ambassador of the above intimating that information that the Peruvian Congress
                    had done likewise would be received with pleasure. You may in your discretion
                    say to President Leguía that the definite termination of this matter would cause
                    gratification to this Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d307-f1" n="19" xml:id="d307-f1-content">
                <p>This paragraph was telegraphed to Brazil, Oct. 30, 6 p.m., as Department’s
                    telegram No. 57 (file No. 721.2315/243b).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
